```python
from dataclasses import dataclass

@dataclass
class Customer:
    customer_id: int
    name: str
    email: str
    tier: str = "standard"

    @property
    def is_premium(self) -> bool:
        return self.tier == "premium"
```
Remove the explicit `customer_id`, `name`, `email`, and `tier` methods; consumers can access attributes directly or via the `is_premium` property.

